and shipped a link authored in the source directory onto a page that renders
somewhere else. I fixed it by rebasing the link, which works, and was the
wrong fix.

`status`, `superseded_by` and `status_note` are three *fields*. `Adr.status`
is one composed reading of them — the right one for an index table, where a
row is all a reader gets. A chain page is not that: the successor is the
**next line on the page**, so linking it in the status says twice what the
shape already says, and the note is an argument about why the step happened,
which is precisely the half this view exists to leave on the document.

