form, the link, and the rebase together.

The lesson generalises past this bug. When a display helper hands you more
than you want and the extra needs *repair* to be safe on your surface, the
question is not how to repair it. It is which field you actually meant. The
composed form is a convenience for one surface; a new surface should ask the
fields what it needs, which is the whole reason [ADR-072](../../record/decisions.d/ADR-072.md) made the note a
field instead of leaving it inside the status string.

This is the second thing in two days where the answer was "the record already
models this, read the narrower field": the first was reading `many` off the
contract instead of guessing a scaffold's shape.

